     "user": "Buildability check: 500 mm wall, 2 m long, 25 mm nozzle, 40 mm/s. Rheometer gives a static yield stress of 0.004 MPa and a structuration rate of 60 Pa per minute.",
     "text": "I’ll check the buildability tool’s required inputs and convert your rheometer values to its units.\n**Verdict: non-printable as an unbraced, single-filament wall under the tool’s default assumptions. Free-wall buckling governs.**\n\nYour measurements convert to **4,000 Pa static yield stress** and **1 Pa/s structuration rate**, treated as values at extrusion.\n\nAssumptions: layer height **12.5 mm**, filament width **29.61 mm**, density **2,100 kg/m³**, stiffness ratio **E/τ = 25**, safety factor **1.5**, and no dwell.\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Printing schedule | 40 layers; 50 s/layer; 33.3 min total |\n| Free-wall buckling | Estimated limit: layer 11, approximately **138 mm** |\n| Plastic collapse | Safety-factored capacity: approximately **23 layers**, below the target |\n| Open time | Cannot assess without your measured open time |\n\nActionable changes:\n\n- **Brace the wall, add returns, or increase wall thickness**, then reassess buckling. Slower printing alone does not establish stability.\n- For plastic stability, the calculated minimum cycle is **123 s/layer**, equivalent to a maximum continuous speed of **16.3 mm/s**. The upper cycle limit requires measured open time.\n- At the current schedule, the tool gives material thresholds of **6,920 Pa initial static yield stress** or **2.46 Pa/s structuration rate**. These address plastic collapse; buckling still requires a separate check.\n\nThe buckling result depends strongly on assumed stiffness and wall restraint. Confirm actual layer dimensions, fresh density, early-age stiffness and open time, then verify experimentally.\n\nFiles: [assessment](</C:/Users/User/3D Printing Concrete Prediction/artifacts/reports/agent/20261017-020455-f45e/assessment_job.md>), [cycle plot](</C:/Users/User/3D Printing Concrete Prediction/artifacts/reports/agent/20261017-020455-f45e/cycle_sweep_job.png>), [cycle data](</C:/Users/User/3D Printing Concrete Prediction/artifacts/reports/agent/20261017-020455-f